[ar:HRV]
[al:Technician Answers - 2026-2030]
[ti:T5 - Electrical Principles]
[00:00.40]Technician answers. T5 - Electrical Principles.
[00:04.82]Group T5A.
[00:06.78]Electrical current is measured in which of the following units? Amperes.
[00:11.48]Electrical power is measured in which of the following units? Watts.
[00:15.97]What is the term for the flow of electrons in an electric circuit? Current.
[00:20.72]What term describes the number of times per second that an alternating current makes a complete cycle? Frequency.
[00:27.87]A difference in which of the following causes electron flow? Voltage.
[00:32.34]What is the unit of frequency? Hertz.
[00:35.17]Why are metals generally good conductors of electricity? They have many free electrons.
[00:40.74]Which of the following is a good electrical insulator? Glass.
[00:44.72]Which of the following describes alternating current? Current that alternates between positive and negative directions.
[00:52.24]Which term describes the rate at which electrical energy is used? Power.
[00:57.13]What type of current flow is opposed by resistance? Direct current; Alternating current; RF current; All these choices are correct.
[01:06.37]Group T5B.
[01:08.40]How many milliamperes is 1.5 amperes? 1500 milliamperes.
[01:14.38]Which is equal to 1,500,000 hertz? 1500 kHz.
[01:20.47]Which is equal to one kilovolt? One thousand volts.
[01:24.11]Which is equal to one microvolt? One one-millionth of a volt.
[01:28.40]Which is equal to 500 milliwatts? 0.5 watts.
[01:32.93]Which is equal to 3000 milliamperes? 3 amperes.
[01:36.89]Which is equal to 3.525 MHz? 3525 kHz.
[01:43.66]Which is equal to 1,000,000 picofarads? 1 microfarad.
[01:47.98]Which decibel value most closely represents a power increase from 5 watts to 10 watts? 3 dB.
[01:54.80]Which decibel value most closely represents a power decrease from 12 watts to 3 watts? -6 dB.
[02:02.19]Which decibel value represents a power increase from 20 watts to 200 watts? 10 dB.
[02:08.81]Which is equal to 28400 kHz? 28.400 MHz.
[02:15.56]Which is equal to 2425 MHz? 2.425 GHz.
[02:22.48]Group T5C.
[02:24.54]What describes the ability to store energy in an electric field? Capacitance.
[02:29.63]What is the unit of capacitance? Farad.
[02:32.52]What describes the ability to store energy in a magnetic field? Inductance.
[02:37.54]What is the unit of inductance? Henry.
[02:40.39]What is the unit of impedance? Ohm.
[02:43.15]What is the abbreviation for kilohertz? kHz.
[02:46.59]What is the abbreviation for megahertz? MHz.
[02:50.06]What formula is used to calculate electrical power (P) in a DC circuit? P = I x E.
[02:56.94]How much power is delivered by a voltage of 13.8 volts DC and a current of 10 amperes? 138 watts.
[03:05.63]How much power is delivered by a voltage of 12 volts DC and a current of 2.5 amperes? 30 watts.
[03:13.40]How much current is required to deliver 120 watts at a voltage of 12 volts DC? 10 amperes.
[03:20.96]What is impedance? The opposition to AC current flow.
[03:25.17]Group T5D.
[03:27.19]What formula is used to calculate current in a circuit? I = E / R.
[03:32.17]What formula is used to calculate voltage in a circuit? E = I x R.
[03:37.52]What formula is used to calculate resistance in a circuit? R = E / I.
[03:42.99]What is the resistance of a circuit in which a current of 3 amperes flows when connected to 90 volts? 30 ohms.
[03:50.74]What is the resistance of a circuit for which the applied voltage is 12 volts and the current flow is 1.5 amperes? 8 ohms.
[03:59.77]What is the resistance of a circuit that draws 4 amperes from a 12-volt source? 3 ohms.
[04:05.80]What is the current in a circuit with an applied voltage of 120 volts and a resistance of 80 ohms? 1.5 amperes.
[04:15.02]What is the current through a 100-ohm resistor connected across 200 volts? 2 amperes.
[04:21.52]What is the current through a 24-ohm resistor connected across 240 volts? 10 amperes.
[04:28.48]What is the voltage across a 2-ohm resistor if a current of 0.5 amperes flows through it? 1 volt.
[04:36.07]What is the voltage across a 10-ohm resistor if a current of 1 ampere flows through it? 10 volts.
[04:42.65]What is the voltage across a 10-ohm resistor if a current of 2 amperes flows through it? 20 volts.
[04:49.33]In which type of circuit is the current always the same through all components? Series.
[04:54.72]In which type of circuit is the voltage always the same across all components? Parallel.
